<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>This import is NOT verified yet: the download has no hard check (no vendor hash, no signature check). A real run is refused by the shared importer until a verification step exists, unless the override sets pcman_allow_unverified to true (the run then publishes with a WARNING, and the report says published, NOT verified). Hands the downloaded Google Earth Pro installer (an EXE) to the package tool (pcman), which publishes it as a new version of the template item into the Cimian repository, or says that nothing is new. For an EXE the package tool is given the version label: the recipe passes the version that the download recipe's WindowsExeVersion step read from the EXE itself (its ProductVersion when that is numbers and dots only, else the four numbers of its fixed file information). The label must equal what a person reads in the file's properties, which the first dry run shows. Whether the package tool has a check of the product for an EXE, like its upgrade code check for an MSI, was NOT established. This recipe was NOT rehearsed with AutoPkg. This is a dry run, which writes nothing, until the recipe's override sets pcman_dry_run to false.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.pcman.GoogleEarthPro</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>GoogleEarthPro</string>
            <key>PCMAN_TEMPLATE</key>
            <string>google-earth-pro</string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>ParentRecipe</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.GoogleEarthPro-Win</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.PcmanProcessors/PcmanImporter</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pathname</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                    <key>pcman_template</key>
                    <string>%PCMAN_TEMPLATE%</string>
                    <key>pcman_version</key>
                    <string>%version%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
